    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 95.93,
      "end_seconds": 98.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.28,
      "text": "I have high cholesterol."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 99.64,
      "end_seconds": 100.34,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "understood"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 103.12,
      "end_seconds": 104.81,
      "duration_seconds": 1.69,
      "text": "I've got migraines."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 106.62,
      "end_seconds": 110.05,
      "duration_seconds": 3.43,
      "text": "alright, migraines, that matches what I have here"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 128.08,
      "end_seconds": 131.26,
      "duration_seconds": 3.18,
      "text": "Do you take any prescribed or over-the-counter medicines?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 132.2,
      "end_seconds": 142.32,
      "duration_seconds": 10.12,
      "text": "I'm on atorvastatin, 20 milligrams, at night. Um, um, I take sumatriptan, 50 milligrams, when needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 143.28,
      "end_seconds": 145.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.59,
      "text": "Have you got any known allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 147.26,
      "end_seconds": 151.95,
      "duration_seconds": 4.69,
      "text": "Um, no, not that I know of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 160.22,
      "end_seconds": 163.82,
      "duration_seconds": 3.6,
      "text": "Okay, and what about dizziness, fever or discharge?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 165.8,
      "end_seconds": 170.99,
      "duration_seconds": 5.19,
      "text": "sorry, what was I saying, none of those, no"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 172.4,
      "end_seconds": 173.99,
      "duration_seconds": 1.59,
      "text": "nothing like ear pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 175.94,
      "end_seconds": 178.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.2,
      "text": "No ear pain, thankfully."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 179.66,
      "end_seconds": 182.02,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "Is your mobility otherwise okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 183.28,
      "end_seconds": 185.53,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "I move fine otherwise."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 186.75,
      "end_seconds": 189.86,
      "duration_seconds": 3.11,
      "text": "time for your numbers, if that's okay"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 200.33,
      "end_seconds": 202.88,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "Bear with me while this finishes..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 212.0,
      "end_seconds": 217.73,
      "duration_seconds": 5.73,
      "text": "okay: temperature is 36.6 degrees, pulse 83, BP is 120 over 77."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 220.45,
      "end_seconds": 223.4,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "let's move on to the examination"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 224.37,
      "end_seconds": 226.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "Raise your arm for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 239.22,
      "end_seconds": 244.33,
      "duration_seconds": 5.11,
      "text": "Both ear drums look dull and retracted with fluid behind them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 247.82,
      "end_seconds": 261.3,
      "duration_seconds": 13.48,
      "text": "You can relax now. Right, here's what I'm thinking. It points towards glue ear. I want to be honest that this is an impression, not a final answer."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 262.75,
      "end_seconds": 265.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.28,
      "text": "Will it clear up?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 266.48,
      "end_seconds": 279.3,
      "duration_seconds": 12.82,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now glue ear is my leading thought, not anything worse. I think a hearing test makes sense here, for reduced hearing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 281.3,
      "end_seconds": 284.02,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "Actually, okay, I'll do it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 285.88,
      "end_seconds": 298.15,
      "duration_seconds": 12.27,
      "text": "we will watch for three months, and sit him at the front of the class the ENT clinic would be the right next step, I'll refer you"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 299.42,
      "end_seconds": 301.36,
      "duration_seconds": 1.94,
      "text": "alright, thank you"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 302.03,
      "end_seconds": 306.26,
      "duration_seconds": 4.23,
      "text": "do get help quickly if the symptoms get worse"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 307.8,
      "end_seconds": 313.7,
      "duration_seconds": 5.9,
      "text": "Let me think, um, okay, I'll look out for that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 315.74,
      "end_seconds": 323.61,
      "duration_seconds": 7.87,
      "text": "Please come and see me in three months. That's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 324.46,
      "end_seconds": 327.25,
